# Who reviews what.
#
# This replaces the squad-named folders. Directories are now named after what they
# run — vote/, worker/, nginx/ — and ownership lives here instead, which is better
# than a folder name because GitHub acts on it: open a PR touching vote/ and Squad B
# is requested as reviewer automatically. That is the "pull requests with peer
# sign-off" the brief asks for, enforced rather than agreed.
#
# Handles below are taken from who actually pushed to each squad branch. Please
# correct your own line if it is wrong — CODEOWNERS only works for people with write
# access to the repository, so anyone missing that will be skipped silently.
#
# Last match wins, so the specific lines override the catch-all.

# Catch-all: the repo lead reviews anything not claimed below.
